The task was to find the maximum area of a rectangle formed by four points from a given set, such that the rectangle has edges parallel to the axes and contains no other points from the set inside or on its border.

I implemented this in `solution.py` by:
1. Iterating through all combinations of 4 points from the input list.
2. Checking if each combination forms a valid rectangle with sides parallel to the axes (exactly two unique x-coordinates and two unique y-coordinates, forming four corners).
3. Verifying that no other point from the input set lies inside or on the border of this rectangle.
4. Keeping track of the maximum area found among all such valid rectangles.

The solution was tested using `run_tests.sh` and passed all tests.
